When an object element’s data attribute is missing or empty, Ladybird
shows the element’s fallback content. Blink does the same: Its
HTMLPlugInElement::RequestObject() fails for an empty URL with no
service type, and HTMLObjectElement::UpdatePluginInternal() then calls
RenderFallbackContent(). WebKit’s HTMLPlugInElement::requestObject()
fails the same way, and HTMLObjectElement::updateWidget() then calls
renderFallbackContent(). And Gecko’s UpdateObjectParameters() in
nsObjectLoadingContent gives an object with no URI and no plugin type
ObjectType::Fallback. Run in Chrome 158, Firefox 151, and WebKit 26.5,
all three show the fallback content for a missing and an empty data
attribute, and once the data attribute is removed from an object.
